  rules: [
    "1️⃣ VERB PATTERNS NIMA?\n\nVerb patterns — bir fe'ldan keyin ikkinchi fe'l qanday shaklda kelishini belgilaydi. Ingliz tilida fe'llardan keyin 4 xil shakl kelishi mumkin:\n\n📌 V-ing (gerund): enjoy, avoid, suggest, finish, mind, practice, keep\n  I enjoy reading. (Men o'qishdan zavqlanaman)\n  She avoids going out late. (U kech chiqishdan qochadi)\n\n📌 to V1 (infinitive): want, need, decide, hope, plan, promise, learn\n  I want to learn English. (Men ingliz tilini o'rganmoqchiman)\n  She needs to study more. (U ko'proq o'qishi kerak)\n\n📌 Person + to V1: tell, ask, want, expect, advise, remind\n  She told me to come. (U menga kelishimni aytdi)\n  He wants you to help. (U sizning yordam berishingizni xohlaydi)\n\n📌 V1 (bare infinitive): modals (can, must, should, might, will)\n  I can swim. (Men suza olaman)\n  You must go. (Siz ketishingiz kerak)\n\n🔴 MUHIM: Fe'lning ma'nosiga qarab, undan keyin V-ing yoki to V1 kelishini BILIB OLISH KERAK!",
    "2️⃣ VERB + V-ING (GERUND)\n\nBa'zi fe'llardan keyin doim V-ing shakli keladi. Bular asosan yoqtirish/yoqtirmaslik va odat fe'llari:\n\n📌 ENJOY — zavqlanmoq:\n  I enjoy reading books. (Men kitob o'qishdan zavqlanaman)\n  She enjoys playing tennis. (U tennis o'ynashdan zavqlanadi)\n\n📌 AVOID — qochmoq:\n  You should avoid eating too much sugar. (Ko'p shakar eyishdan qochishingiz kerak)\n  She avoids going out alone at night. (U kechasi yolg'iz chiqishdan qochadi)\n\n📌 SUGGEST — taklif qilmoq:\n  I suggest taking a break. (Tanaffus qilishni taklif qilaman)\n  He suggested going to the park. (U parkka borishni taklif qildi)\n\n📌 FINISH — tugatmoq:\n  I finished writing the report. (Hisobot yozishni tugatdim)\n  Have you finished eating? (Ovqatlanishni tugatdingizmi?)\n\n📌 MIND — qarshi bo'lmoq (savol/inkor):\n  Do you mind waiting for a moment? (Bir oz kutishga qarshimisiz?)\n  I don't mind helping you. (Sizga yordam berishga qarshi emasman)\n\n📌 PRACTICE — mashq qilmoq:\n  You need to practice speaking English. (Ingliz tilida gapirishni mashq qilishingiz kerak)\n\n📌 KEEP — davom ettirmoq:\n  Keep trying! (Harakat qilishda davom et!)\n  She keeps making the same mistake. (U bir xil xatoni qilishda davom etadi)",
    "3️⃣ VERB + TO V1 (INFINITIVE)\n\nBa'zi fe'llardan keyin doim 'to' bilan infinitive keladi:\n\n📌 WANT — xohlamoq:\n  I want to learn Spanish. (Men ispan tilini o'rganmoqchiman)\n  She wants to become a doctor. (U shifokor bo'lishni xohlaydi)\n\n📌 NEED — kerak bo'lmoq:\n  I need to go now. (Men hozir ketishim kerak)\n  You need to study harder. (Ko'proq o'qishing kerak)\n\n📌 DECIDE — qaror qilmoq:\n  I decided to move to Tashkent. (Men Toshkentga ko'chishga qaror qildim)\n\n📌 HOPE — umid qilmoq:\n  I hope to see you soon. (Sizni tez orada ko'rishga umid qilaman)\n\n📌 PLAN — rejalashtirmoq:\n  We plan to visit Samarkand next summer. (Kelasi yozda Samarqandga borishni rejalashtiryapmiz)\n\n📌 PROMISE — va'da bermoq:\n  I promise to help you. (Sizga yordam berishga va'da beraman)\n\n📌 LEARN — o'rganmoq:\n  I am learning to drive. (Men haydashni o'rganyapman)\n\n📌 WOULD LIKE — xohlamoq (muloyim):\n  I would like to order coffee. (Men kofe buyurtma qilmoqchiman)\n\n🔴 ESLATMA: 'Want' va 'Would like' o'xshash, lekin 'would like' muloyimroq.",
    "4️⃣ VERB + PERSON + TO V1\n\nBa'zi fe'llar orqali biror kimsaga biror narsa qilishni aytamiz:\n\n📌 TELL + person + to V1:\n  She told me to come early. (U menga erta kelishimni aytdi)\n  The teacher told us to open our books. (O'qituvchi bizga kitoblarni ochishimizni aytdi)\n\n📌 ASK + person + to V1:\n  He asked me to help him. (U mendan yordam so'radi)\n  She asked us to wait. (U bizdan kutishimizni so'radi)\n\n📌 WANT + person + to V1:\n  I want you to be happy. (Men sening baxtli bo'lishingni xohlayman)\n  She wants her children to study well. (U bolalarining yaxshi o'qishini xohlaydi)\n\n📌 EXPECT + person + to V1:\n  I expect you to do your best. (Men sendan qo'lingdan kelganini qilishingni kutaman)\n\n📌 ADVISE + person + to V1:\n  The doctor advised me to rest. (Shifokor menga dam olishni maslahat berdi)\n\n📌 REMIND + person + to V1:\n  Please remind me to call her. (Iltimos, unga qo'ng'iroq qilishni eslat)\n\n📌 INKOR: He told me NOT to come. (U menga kelmaslikni aytdi)\n  She asked us NOT to be late. (U bizdan kechikmaslikni so'radi)",
    "5️⃣ VERB + V1 (BARE INFINITIVE — MODALLAR)\n\nModal fe'llardan keyin doim 'to'siz infinitive (V1) keladi:\n\n📌 CAN:\n  I can swim. (Men suza olaman)\n  She can speak three languages. (U uch tilda gapira oladi)\n\n📌 MUST:\n  You must wear a seatbelt. (Xavfsizlik kamarini taqishingiz kerak)\n  Students must do their homework. (O'quvchilar uy vazifasini qilishlari kerak)\n\n📌 SHOULD:\n  You should drink more water. (Ko'proq suv ichishingiz kerak)\n  She should see a doctor. (U shifokorga ko'rinishi kerak)\n\n📌 MIGHT:\n  It might rain today. (Bugun yomg'ir yog'ishi mumkin)\n  She might come to the party. (U ziyofatga kelishi mumkin)\n\n📌 WILL:\n  I will help you. (Men sizga yordam beraman)\n\n🔴 MUHIM: Modallardan keyin 'to' QO'SHILMAYDI!\n  ✅ I can swim. ❌ I can to swim.\n  ✅ You must go. ❌ You must to go.\n  ✅ She should study. ❌ She should to study.",
    "6️⃣ LIKE / LOVE / HATE + V-ING YOKI TO V1\n\nLike, love, hate, prefer — ikkala shaklni ham qabul qiladi, ma'no deyarli bir xil:\n\n📌 LIKE + V-ing = umumiy yoqtirish:\n  I like reading books. (Men kitob o'qishni yaxshi ko'raman — umuman)\n\n📌 LIKE + to V1 = muayyan holatda:\n  I like to read before bed. (Men uxlashdan oldin o'qishni yaxshi ko'raman — odat)\n\n📌 LOVE + V-ing / to V1:\n  I love swimming. = I love to swim. (Men suzishni yaxshi ko'raman)\n\n📌 HATE + V-ing / to V1:\n  I hate getting up early. = I hate to get up early. (Men erta turishni yomon ko'raman)\n\n🔴 FARQ (kichik nuances):\n  I like swimming. (Umuman suzishni yoqtiraman)\n  I like to swim every morning. (Har kuni ertalab suzishni yoqtiraman — ancha odat)\n\n📌 WOULD LIKE (xohlamoq) — faqat to V1:\n  I would like to order now. (Men hozir buyurtma qilmoqchiman)\n  ❌ I would like ordering now.",
    "7️⃣ KO'P UCHRAYDIGAN XATOLAR\n\n🔴 XATO 1 — 'To' ni unutish:\n  ❌ I want go home.\n  ✅ I want to go home.\n\n🔴 XATO 2 — Modal + to:\n  ❌ I can to swim.\n  ✅ I can swim.\n\n🔴 XATO 3 — Gerund o'rniga infinitive:\n  ❌ I enjoy to read.\n  ✅ I enjoy reading.\n\n🔴 XATO 4 — Person + to da 'to' ni unutish:\n  ❌ She told me come.\n  ✅ She told me to come.\n\n🔴 XATO 5 — Suggest + to:\n  ❌ I suggest to take a break.\n  ✅ I suggest taking a break.\n\n🔴 XATO 6 — 'To' ni noto'g'ri joylashtirish:\n  ❌ I want that you help me.\n  ✅ I want you to help me.\n\n🔴 XATO 7 — Would like + V-ing:\n  ❌ I would like going home.\n  ✅ I would like to go home.",
  ],
